---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const p='/equipment/05-04/';
const manual='https://www.equipx.net/uploads/JAWoollam/JAWoollamalpha-SE-Manual-Hardware.pdf', brochure='https://qd-uki.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/alpha-se-brochure-2022.pdf';
const refs=[['front','Source and detector arms','Legacy product photograph establishes left source, right detector, silver pivoting arms and square green power switch.',brochure+'#page=1'],['chuck','Standard reflection stage','Legacy manual Fig. 3-4 and Fig. 4-1: removable standard chuck, hold-down line and central support; optical spacing estimated.',manual+'#page=20'],['side','Side and carry slots','Manual Fig. 3-1 front and side establishes base footprint and height. Rear fitting hardware exists; positions and internal geometry are inferred.',manual+'#page=18'],['rear','Rear utility panel','Hardware manual §3.2 establishes IEC inlet and USB host link, not the reconstructed positions. Rear arrangement is illustrative.',manual+'#page=18']];
---
<Layout pageTitle="alpha-SE · spectroscopic ellipsometry" description="Operate a metric alpha-SE and fit dielectric film thickness from Ψ and Δ, including a single-wavelength ambiguity test." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment alpha">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/05-04/">← Equipment 05-04</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#as-ref">References</a><a href="#as-tests">Verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">05-04 · OPTICAL THIN FILM METROLOGY</span><h2>J.A. Woollam alpha-SE</h2><p>Operate the legacy rotating-compensator alpha-SE, not its alpha 2.0 successor. The selected version uses its standard reflection optics and vacuum chuck, without the focus probe, camera or transmission holder.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><span class="eq-meta">01 / INSPECT</span><h3>Optical head and specimen</h3><div id="as-model" aria-label="Orbitable alpha-SE with independently indexed source and detector arms"></div><div class="bar">{['Overall','Front','Chuck','Side','Rear'].map(x=><button data-as-view={x}>{x}</button>)}<button id="as-vr" hidden>Enter VR</button></div><p id="as-view" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p class="small">Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. Select the source/detector indexers to cycle their angles. Violet guide lines mark nominal beam paths and are not a measured image.</p></section>
<section><span class="eq-meta">02 / MEASURE</span><h3>Film and incidence settings</h3><div class="bar"><button id="as-power">Power on</button><button id="as-vacuum">Vacuum on</button><button id="as-load">Unload film</button></div>
<div class="config"><label>Source index<select id="as-source">{[65,70,75,90].map(x=><option value={x}>{x}°</option>)}</select></label><label>Detector index<select id="as-detector">{[65,70,75,90].map(x=><option value={x}>{x}°</option>)}</select></label>
<label>Virtual film thickness (nm)<input id="as-thickness" type="number" min="0" max="2000" step="any" value="123.4"/></label><label>Virtual dielectric n<input id="as-index" type="number" min="1" max="8" step="any" value="1.46"/></label>
<label>Fit upper bound (nm)<input id="as-max" type="number" step="any" min="1" max="2000" value="1000"/></label><label>Spectrum in fit<select id="as-mode"><option value="full">All observed wavelengths and angles</option><option value="single">Single datum near 600 nm, 70° if present</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button id="as-acquire">Acquire reflected spectrum</button><button id="as-fit" class="primary">Fit film thickness</button><button id="as-reference">Restore independent 123.4 nm reference</button></div><p id="as-status" aria-live="polite">Loading independent reference…</p>
<details><summary>Import or inspect a spectrum</summary><p>Upload <code>bts.ellipsometry-spectrum.v1</code> with unique angle/wavelength rows. A supplied stack may have 1–4 finite layers with fixed constant or tabulated n,k. Only the first layer thickness is fitted.</p><input type="file" id="as-import" accept=".json,application/json" aria-label="Spectrum JSON"/><p><a href={p+'independent-spectrum.json'}>Independent example</a> · <a href={p+'contract.schema.json'}>Data contract</a></p></details></section></div>
<section><span class="eq-meta">03 / ESTIMATE</span><h3>Polarization and thickness ambiguity</h3><div class="grid"><div><canvas id="as-residual" width="700" height="300" aria-label="Angular residuals versus wavelength"></canvas><canvas id="as-profile" width="700" height="270" aria-label="Thickness profile objective with alternate minima"></canvas></div><div><output id="as-results">No fit.</output><div class="bar"><button id="as-json" disabled>Export fitted revision</button><button id="as-csv" disabled>Export residuals CSV</button><button id="as-spectrum" disabled>Export input spectrum</button></div></div></div></section>
<section><h3>How the fit works</h3><p>For each wavelength and incidence angle, the simulator recursively combines coherent Fresnel reflection coefficients using the passive index n + ik. The complex ratio r<sub>p</sub>/r<sub>s</sub> gives Ψ from the amplitude ratio and Δ from the argument. Both reflection bases are defined consistently, with opposite normal-incidence signs; Δ is wrapped into [0°,360°). Phase is unset if either amplitude vanishes. The search profiles thickness globally over the displayed interval, refines local minima and uses circular Δ residuals.</p>
<p><strong>Try this:</strong> fit the preloaded 81-sample reference (27 wavelengths at 65°, 70° and 75°). Then restrict to the single datum. Similar residual minima repeat because an integer round trip in optical phase leaves the single-wavelength reflection unchanged. If film and substrate indices match at every wavelength, thickness is optically invisible. The reported alternate minima lie within a 0.1° RMS agreement threshold, not a confidence interval. Changing assumed optical constants can shift thickness without a unique answer.</p>
<p><strong>Limits:</strong> planar isotropic layers, flat interfaces and semi-infinite substrate only. No roughness, backside reflection, instrument noise, CCD fitting, polarization calibration or transmission solver. The constants in the reference case represent a synthetic optical contrast, not measured SiO₂/Si data. Imported origins are not independently verified. No compatible downstream ellipsometry-result consumer was found; the machine-readable contract and a fitted example are provided.</p></section>
<section id="as-ref"><span class="eq-meta">04 / EVIDENCE</span><h3>Reference sheet</h3><p>Original reconstructions alongside links to the specific hardware or drawing. Envelope dimensions are nominal; detail geometry and exact serial revision are not verified.</p>
<div class="figs">{refs.map(([id,title,d,u])=><figure><img src={p+id+'.webp'} loading="lazy" alt={'Original alpha-SE reconstruction: '+title}/><figcaption><b>{title}.</b> {d} <a href={u}>Original source</a></figcaption></figure>)}</div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value and scope</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Nominal dimensions W × H × D</td><td>480 × 300 × 310 mm in the legacy hardware drawing, 90° inspection pose.</td><td><a href="https://www.easymanua.ls/j-a-woollam/alpha-se/manual?p=18">Fig. 3-1, printed p. 3-2</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Access and holding</td><td>Up to 200 mm diameter, 16 mm thickness; selected standard chuck and virtual 82 mm illustration, not a factory chuck diameter claim.</td><td><a href={brochure}>Legacy specifications</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Source and detector</td><td>Quartz tungsten halogen and rotating compensator/CCD; 380–900 nm, 180 nominal wavelengths. Lab accepts 1–180 values per reflection angle, not the exact factory wavelength grid.</td><td><a href={brochure}>Legacy specifications</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Angle detents</td><td>Manual 65°, 70°, 75° reflection; 90° straight-through inspection only. Both indexes must align.</td><td><a href="https://www.easymanua.ls/j-a-woollam/alpha-se/manual?p=34">Manual Fig. 4-1 through 4-4</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Acquisition modes</td><td>Hardware lists 3, 10 or 30 seconds; instantaneous synthetic calculation is not emulation.</td><td><a href={brochure}>Legacy specifications</a></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p><a href="https://aggiefab.tamu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/SOP_Wollam-Ellipsometer.pdf">Institutional installed instrument and controls</a></p></section>
<section id="as-tests"><span class="eq-meta">05 / VERIFICATION</span><h3>Independent checks</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Bare 1.5 dielectric at normal incidence</td><td>rₛ −0.2, rₚ +0.2</td><td>−0.2, +0.2</td><td>10⁻¹⁰</td></tr>
<tr><td>Independent 81-point matrix fixture</td><td>123.4 nm</td><td>123.4000 nm</td><td>±0.02 nm</td></tr>
<tr><td>Single wavelength (600 nm / 70°)</td><td>Repeating model minima</td><td>Multiple thickness orders</td><td>0.02 nm in repeat spacing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Nonmatched indexers</td><td>Reject acquisition</td><td>Rejected</td><td>Exact</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p><a href={p+'reference-cases.json'}>Declared test cases</a> · <a href={p+'verification.json'}>Verification report</a> · <a href={p+'fit-example.json'}>Fit example</a> · <a href={p+'alpha-se.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={p+'model.py'} download>Editable model</a> · <a href={p+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR interaction anchors</a></p><p class="small">The VR adapter uses the same actions and physically scaled instrument. No headset test or hardware comparison is claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
